REPAIR: 178 phantom deletions from an armed-index race, restored verbatim from HEAD~1

This is a repair commit and it exists because commit `591f6b499` (`TWORED`) carried **435 changed files**
and `delete mode 100644 gates/README.md` while my `--only` named **one** path.

**MEASURED BEFORE REPAIRING:** `HEAD~1` **7 435** files, `HEAD` **7 505**, **182 LOST**, **252 ADDED**,
**AND ALL **182** EXIST ON DISK** -- i.e. **182 PHANTOM DELETIONS, ZERO WORK LOST.**

**OF THE 182: **178 ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL TO `HEAD~1`** AND ARE RESTORED HERE VERBATIM. **THE **4** THAT DIFFER ARE
LIVE WORK AND ARE **NOT** IN THIS COMMIT**: `gates/assertlit.rows`, `gates/falseclaim.rows`,
`gates/gates-pop.py`, `gates/oracleblind.rows` -- `gates-pop.py` BEING EDITED **AT THE MOMENT** OF THE MEASUREMENT.

**THIS IS THE `AGENTS.md` HAZARD THAT WEEKS OF BRIEFING HAVE DESCRIBED AND THAT NOBODY HAD SEEN FIRE ON A CALLER's
OWN COMMIT:** `jj` COLOCATES INTO GIT's INDEX ON EVERY SNAPSHOT, AN INTENT-TO-ADD PLACEHOLDER ANSWERS `e69de29b`,
AND **A CONCURRENT AGENT's INDEX STATE LANDED IN A `--only` COMMIT THAT NAMED ONE PATH.**

**THE LESSON IS NOT "BE CAREFUL". IT IS THAT **`--only` IS NOT A BOUNDARY AGAINST A CONTAMINATED INDEX** -- SO A
COMMIT's `--stat` IS THE CHECK, AND `435 FILES CHANGED` ON A ONE-PATH `--only` IS THE SIGNAL THAT SOMETHING IS
WRONG AND THE COMMIT SHOULD BE INSPECTED BEFORE THE NEXT ONE IS MADE.**

